.\docs\carbon_calibration.md:1:# Carbon Calibration Model
.\docs\carbon_calibration.md:3:This repository includes a calibrated carbon subsystem in `carbon_model.py` with calibration data in `carbon_calib.json`.
.\docs\carbon_calibration.md:7:- **Operational carbon** is calibrated from measured/estimated energy and a grid emission factor.
.\docs\carbon_calibration.md:8:- **Embodied carbon** is a **proxy-calibrated** estimate from effective area, node intensity defaults, and yield assumptions.
.\docs\carbon_calibration.md:13:- **Static carbon (embodied/manufacturing proxy):**
.\docs\carbon_calibration.md:14:  - `static_carbon_kgco2e = area_cm2 * fab_intensity_kgco2e_per_cm2 * yield_loss_factor`
.\docs\carbon_calibration.md:15:- **Dynamic carbon (operational/use-phase):**
.\docs\carbon_calibration.md:16:  - `energy_kwh = energy_joules / 3.6e6`
.\docs\carbon_calibration.md:17:  - `dynamic_carbon_kgco2e = energy_kwh * grid_factor_kgco2e_per_kwh`
.\docs\carbon_calibration.md:19:  - `total_carbon_kgco2e = static_carbon_kgco2e + dynamic_carbon_kgco2e_lifetime`
.\docs\carbon_calibration.md:23:`carbon_calib.json` provides:
.\docs\carbon_calibration.md:29:  - `design_area_multiplier` (currently 1.0 across nodes; placeholder to keep area scaling explicit)
.\docs\carbon_calibration.md:33:  - scenario-only best/worst factors used for stress envelopes (not region averages)
.\docs\carbon_calibration.md:38:## Node and area assumptions transparency
.\docs\carbon_calibration.md:40:When a node is not directly calibrated (for example 14nm), the model maps to the nearest calibrated node and reports:
.\docs\carbon_calibration.md:46:Area assumptions report whether area was direct input or derived from a memory-bit proxy (`area_source`, `area_proxy_used`).
.\docs\carbon_calibration.md:50:`estimate_carbon_bounds(...)` returns separate concepts:
.\docs\carbon_calibration.md:54:- `best_case`: scenario minimums using greener grid and lower node/yield intensity assumptions
.\docs\carbon_calibration.md:57:Uncertainty bounds are not equivalent to scenario best/worst envelopes.
.\docs\carbon_calibration.md:61:`ecc_selector.select(...)` supports optional carbon policies (default behavior unchanged when omitted or `None`):
.\docs\carbon_calibration.md:63:- `minimum_total_carbon`
.\docs\carbon_calibration.md:64:- `minimum_dynamic_carbon`
.\docs\carbon_calibration.md:65:- `minimum_static_carbon`
.\docs\carbon_calibration.md:66:- `balanced_carbon_energy`
.\docs\carbon_calibration.md:68:With a carbon policy, candidate records include:
.\docs\carbon_calibration.md:70:- `static_carbon_kgco2e`
.\docs\carbon_calibration.md:71:- `dynamic_carbon_kgco2e`
.\docs\carbon_calibration.md:72:- `carbon_bounds`
.\docs\carbon_calibration.md:76:`eccsim.py carbon` preserves legacy formatting by default.
.\docs\carbon_calibration.md:78:Use `--calibrated` to emit a JSON payload containing nominal/best/worst calibrated results and score breakdown, while still including legacy values.
