.\docs\RESULTS_AND_INTERPRETATION.md:96:The current research contribution is therefore a software/evidence result: extensible identity handling, exact functional verification with negative-result retention, automatic fair normalization, and scenario-aware analytical selection. The strongest missing result is equally important: there is no physical winner, no same-code physical PPA comparison, no MUX/controller or transition measurement, and no reproducible physical adaptive break-even.
.\docs\SAFEFORGE_EXPERIMENTAL_PROTOCOL.md:3:No hardware measurement is fabricated in this repository. The exact human experiment still required is:
.\docs\SAFEFORGE_EXPERIMENTAL_PROTOCOL.md:18:For controlled replay, load each emitted `positions` vector into the declared word through the board-specific injector, decode with the frozen generated policy, and record corrected/DUE/SDC plus latency. Keep injected replay (evidence level B) separate from naturally observed raw events (level A). Train/compile on all but one device/voltage/source group; evaluate the held-out group once without target, radius, placement, or policy retuning.
.\docs\SAFEFORGE_METHOD.md:3:SafeForge is a finite-support, distributionally robust compiler for SRAM ECC policies. Given a systematic binary matrix, a nominal conditional fault PMF, an expanded bit-exact error support, and an explicit ambiguity set, it executes the actual decoder for every error vector and compiles each nonzero syndrome to either `correct(error_vector)` or deliberate `DUE`.
.\docs\SAFEFORGE_METHOD.md:25:For `r <= 4` and zero SDC, exact co-synthesis enumerates every ordered selection of distinct nonzero, non-basis systematic data columns. For each matrix it constructs the maximal action set that is SDC-free for every PMF on the declared support, then applies the safety-first hierarchy. The search visits all 7,920 `(8,4)` ordered candidates and proves optimality within that explicit scope.
.\docs\SAFEFORGE_METHOD.md:27:For 64 data bits, arbitrary-matrix co-synthesis is retained as a negative scalability result. Practical evaluation fixes conventional extended-Hamming SECDED, Hsiao SECDED, or an existing generated `(72,64)` matrix and compiles decisions over its 255 nonzero syndrome classes. The frozen deterministic class rule generates certified feasible SDC-DUE operating points. It is not presented as a globally optimal constrained frontier. The physical-column mapping search remains a verified heuristic, not a global optimum.
.\docs\SAFEFORGE_METHOD.md:35:Generated SystemVerilog contains the encoder/syndrome network, correction-mask/action table, abstain/DUE signal, 128-bit safety-envelope identifier, envelope-valid input, fallback selection, and no-certified-mode signal. The validation runner archives Icarus execution, Verilator lint, and Yosys/ABC generic cell/depth reports with exact versions and commands. Structural XOR/table and generic-cell counts are not physical area, timing, power, or PPA. Physical claims require a characterized library and synthesis/place-and-route flow.
