.\docs\RELIABILITY_AND_ERROR_MODELS.md:86:In the multi-ECC scenario study, voltage scales dynamic bit/XOR energy with \(V^2\). Temperature linearly interpolates a configured leakage multiplier between 25 °C and 85 °C. Neither changes exact decoder behavior. In the legacy leakage model, current density approximately doubles every 15 °C. These are model assumptions with bounded configured ranges, not measurements.
